  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 235 PM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nFriday night through Tuesday:\n\n500 mb cluster analysis generally shows an anomalous 500 mb \nridge axis developing over the region Friday night into Saturday\nnight, before becoming more zonal Sunday into Monday. This \nshould result in south winds maintaining warm temperatures into \nthe weekend. There may finally be a cold front that shifts \nslowly southeast across the region Sunday into Sunday night or \nMonday. This may have enough moisture and upward vertical motion\nwith it to bring 20 to 30 percent chances for showers. \n\nCold air advection behind the front with north to northeast \nwinds may bring cooler and more seasonable temperatures for \nearly next week. This is supported by ensemble member trends.\n\nWood",
